{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1463515601,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY2MzUyNjY1Nw=="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1463736079,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDU1NzU0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-220557548"},"message":"I think it is a good idea to allow for a similar way of a config command as git has and address items the same way. Therefore I'd vote for the same config file format as well. As a tool on top of git/annex, datalad should be usable and configurable the same way. So: \nQ1: git way (probably using gitpython config reader/writer)\nQ3: Yes, think so to. `-c` option like git, also allowing for passing git and annex options. And probably a `datalad config` command similar to git.\nQ2: I'm fine with your approach in case of git format.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463751109,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDYwNjE4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-220606180"},"message":"Q1: Git\nQ2: Let's stay close to git also. Semantic units in a variable name separated by dots, and '_' used to replace them for envvars.\nQ3: what Ben said. ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463751901,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDYwOTM1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-220609358"},"message":"In terms of files to read: We should do the same as git-annex:\n1. .git/config for repo- and clone-specific config, not intended to be propagated\n2. .gitattributes for per-path config stuff that should go with the dataset when published.\n\nEven for a user-config the main git config files makes most sense.\n\nWe may need to add a .datalad/config file in a dataset for other publishable configuration items -- if we can come up with necessary ones.\n\nPrefix would be `datalad`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1463752400,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDYxMTQyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-220611429"},"message":"\u003e    In terms of files to read: We should do the same as git-annex:\n\u003e     1. .git/config for repo- and clone-specific config, not intended to be\n\u003e        propagated\n\u003e     2. .gitattributes for per-path config stuff that should go with the\n\u003e        dataset when published.\n\u003e    Even for a user-config the main git config files makes most sense.\n\u003e    We may need to add a .datalad/config file in a dataset for other\n\u003e    publishable configuration items -- if we can come up with necessary ones.\n\nyes -- we would need some custom location as well, outside of .git/,\nsince some configuration/settings might not be appropriate for\n.gitattributes but need to be committed.  E.g. configuration or entire\npipelines for crawling, and status files.  See e.g. how it is now\n\nhttp://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000001/.datalad/crawl/","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1463752518,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDYxMTkyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-220611923"},"message":"and https://github.com/datalad/ratholeradio-archive/tree/master/.datalad/crawl/pipelines  where entire .py crawling pipeline is provided  (crawl assumes path `.datalad/crawl/pipelines`) to look for a pipeline ATM.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1469118052,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNDMwNjA3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-234306077"},"message":"Just a note TODO:  check if git config format allows multiline entries as we use already somewhat in some config files.... might be somewhat of a blow","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1470159612,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4MjI0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236982241"},"message":"@yarikoptic git config format does not allow for multiline values.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1470159982,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4NDEyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236984126"},"message":"@yarikoptic However, escaped newlines (`\\n`) are supported and are correctly expanded via `git config` calls.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1470160125,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4NDgwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236984805"},"message":"@yarikoptic git config files support inclusion of other files. Quote from manpage:\n\n```\n      You can include one config file from another by setting the\n       special include.path variable to the name of the file to be\n       included. The included file is expanded immediately, as if its\n       contents had been found at the location of the include directive.\n       If the value of the include.path variable is a relative path, the\n       path is considered to be relative to the configuration file in\n       which the include directive was found. The value of include.path\n       is subject to tilde expansion: ~/ is expanded to the value of\n       $HOME, and ~user/ to the specified user’s home directory. See\n       below for examples.\n\n           [include]\n                   path = /path/to/foo.inc ; include by absolute path\n                   path = foo ; expand \"foo\" relative to the current file\n                   path = ~/foo ; expand \"foo\" in your $HOME directory\n\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1470160448,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4NjUwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236986505"},"message":"On Tue, 02 Aug 2016, Michael Hanke wrote:\n\n\u003e    @yarikoptic git config files support inclusion of other files. Quote from\n\u003e    manpage:\n\nnice... one feature in python configs I have used before but no longer (I\nthink) is the string interpolations.  but once again I don't think we would\nneed it.  as for new lines -- I rely on that feature e.g. to separate fields\nspecification for authentication forms, and multiple regexes for urls see e.g.\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/datalad/downloaders/configs/crcns.cfg\nsure thing could be worked around somehow with git config, but not yet sure\nwhat could be the best way (dedicated uniqely named section with all the fields\nor what)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1470160579,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4NzE2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236987161"},"message":"Using `\\n` as field separator would work, just not without escapes. It would be\n\n```\nhtml_form_fields = username={user}\\n\\\n                   password={password}\\n\\\n                   submit=Login\\n\\\n                   fn=alm-1/filelist.txt\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1470161040,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk4OTY1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236989659"},"message":"Michael Hanke wrote:\n\n\u003e @yarikoptic git config format does not allow for multiline values.\n\nActually...\n\n```\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/r\u003egit config foo.bar line1\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/r\u003egit config --add foo.bar line2\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/r\u003egit config --get-all foo.bar\nline1\nline2\n```\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1470161446,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjk5MTc0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-236991747"},"message":"@joeyh Indeed, thanks!\n\n```\ngit config -f sometest.cfg --add datalad.creds username=some\ngit config -f sometest.cfg --add datalad.creds passwd=password1\ncat sometest.cfg\n[datalad]\n    creds = username=some\n    creds = passwd=password1\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473172504,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDk2OTk0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/437#issuecomment-244969943"},"message":"We went for Git's config and the implementation is now in master (from #744)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473172504,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Nzc5NDMxMjA0"},"status":2}]}